<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raden Patah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1455–1518</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raden Patah was the founder and first sultan of Demak, the first Muslim sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, in the late 15th century. Javanese tradition makes him a son of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> king and a Chinese mother. Supported by the Muslim saints known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wali-songo">Wali Songo</a>, he made Demak the leading power on Java's north coast as Majapahit declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raden-patah.jpg" alt="Raden Patah" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mhatopzz · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MUS_Koin_Sultan_Pangeran_Raden_Fatah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
